  "rhythm": "Songsterr s385697 (the full-band tab, a track per player) at its 105 BPM: Chester Bennington's vocal track, bars 24 beat 2.5 to 32, note for note, the 3-3-2 syncopations and sixteenths as written (a sixteenth is 0.143 s, over the ocarina's minimum, so full speed), rests kept; the last note held a beat longer to ring out. 35.5 beats = 20.3 s. Poodleskirt asked for the first three notes alone: the drums, bass and parts start on the fourth note (bar 25's downbeat), so those three have no drum hit by design; every later ocarina, bass and part onset sits on one. Band from the tab, all +6: Rob Bourdon's drum track (kick, snare, hats, crashes; the overdub track left out) with quiet closed hats on 14 sixteenths only the others play; the pick bass an octave up (G2..G3); parts: the distorted guitar's held power chords (soft), the guitar harmonics an octave up, above the ocarina (soft), and the sampler's string pad (softest). The piano riff isn't in the chorus. General MIDI sound font (distorted guitar).",
